From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isoriano1968 <81116077+isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 18700 applesmc: fan minimum writes, smcfan(8) presets

applesmc(4D) gets one write path: APPLESMC_IOC_WRITE, for privileged
callers (sys_config) and only for F<n>Mn and F<n>Tg of type fpe2, clamped
to [the F<n>Mn found at attach, F<n>Mx]. The original minimum of every
fan written is restored at detach; APPLESMC_IOC_FANMIN returns it.
The write protocol is the one of Linux applesmc.c write_smc().

smcfan(8) lists the fans and sets the presets auto, cool, cooler, max
or an explicit minimum; svc:/system/applesmc-fan applies config/preset
at boot, and the rights profile "Apple SMC Fan Control" lets a user
run it with pfexec.
