+.Dd November 14, 2026
+.Dt SMCFAN 8
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm smcfan
+.Nd fan presets for an Intel Mac
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+.Nm
+.Nm
+.Op Fl p
+.Fl s Ar preset
+.Nm
+.Fl m Ar rpm
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+utility sets how fast the fans of an Intel-based Apple Macintosh turn at
+least, through
+.Xr applesmc 4D .
+It only raises the minimum speed
+.Pq key Sy F Ns Ar n Ns Sy Mn
+of every fan; the System Management Controller keeps controlling the fans
+above that minimum, with its own thermal protection, and never lets them
+turn slower.
+.Pp
+Without options
+.Nm
+lists every fan the driver can set with its current speed, the target the
+SMC chose, the minimum, the maximum and the default minimum
+.Pq the minimum when the driver attached ,
+all in RPM, followed by a line
+.Ql preset: name
+naming the preset all fans are at, or
+.Sy manual .
+Listing needs no privileges.
+.Pp
+The presets are, for every fan:
+.Bl -tag -width "cooler"
+.It Sy auto
+The default minimum: the fans are the SMC's alone.
+.It Sy cool
+The default minimum plus one third of the way to the maximum.
+.It Sy cooler
+The default minimum plus two thirds of the way to the maximum.
+.It Sy max
+The maximum.
+.El
+.Pp
+A preset lasts until the next preset, until the driver is unloaded
+.Pq which restores the default minimum
+or until the machine restarts.
+The service
+.Sy svc:/system/applesmc-fan:default
+applies the preset in the property
+.Sy config/preset
+.Pq default Sy auto
+at boot, and sets
+.Sy auto
+when it is disabled.
+.Sh OPTIONS
+.Bl -tag -width Fl
+.It Fl m Ar rpm
+Set the minimum of every fan to
+.Ar rpm .
+The driver limits it to the range from the default minimum to the maximum;
+.Nm
+says so when it does.
+.It Fl p
+With
+.Fl s ,
+also keep the preset: set
+.Sy config/preset
+of the service
+.Sy svc:/system/applesmc-fan ,
+then refresh and enable its instance
+.Sy default .
+.It Fl s Ar preset
+Set
+.Ar preset :
+.Sy auto ,
+.Sy cool ,
+.Sy cooler
+or
+.Sy max .
+.El
+.Pp
+Setting the fans needs the
+.Sy sys_config
+privilege; the rights profile
+.Sy Apple SMC Fan Control
+lets a user do it with
+.Xr pfexec 1 .
+.Sh FILES
+.Bl -tag -width Pa
+.It Pa /dev/applesmc
+SMC device.
+.It Pa /etc/security/exec_attr.d/applesmc
+.It Pa /etc/security/prof_attr.d/applesmc
+The rights profile
+.Sy Apple SMC Fan Control .
+.El
+.Sh EXIT STATUS
+.Bl -tag -width Sy
+.It Sy 0
+Successful completion.
+.It Sy 1
+An error occurred.
+.It Sy 2
+Invalid command line options were specified.
+.It Sy 3
+There is no SMC, the driver is not loaded, or it cannot set the fans.
+.It Sy 4
+The caller is not privileged to set the fans.
+.El
+.Sh EXAMPLES
+.Bl -tag -width 0n
+.It Sy Example 1 No Fans and preset
+.Bd -literal
+$ smcfan
+FAN      RPM  TARGET     MIN     MAX  DEFAULT
+F0       926     926     790    1900      790
+preset: auto
+.Ed
+.It Sy Example 2 No Cooler from now on, also after a restart
+.Bd -literal
+$ pfexec smcfan -p -s cooler
+.Ed
+.It Sy Example 3 No Give a user the rights profile
+.Bd -literal
+# usermod -P +"Apple SMC Fan Control" user
+.Ed
+.El
+.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
+The command line is
+.Sy Uncommitted .
+The output is
+.Sy Not-An-Interface ,
+except for the
+.Sy preset :
+line, which is
+.Sy Uncommitted .
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr pfexec 1 ,
+.Xr applesmc 4D ,
+.Xr smf 7 ,
+.Xr smcstat 8 ,
+.Xr usermod 8
